t</h2><p class="gd-p">Sometimes we need to change your booking, for example another car of the same class. You decide.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">You get an email, and your booking says &quot;We suggest a change to your booking&quot;. Press <b class="gd-ui">Review and answer</b>.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Read what changes (before and after), the reason, the money and the time left to answer.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">To agree, press <b class="gd-ui">Accept and sign the amendment</b>, sign, then press <b class="gd-ui">Accept and sign</b>.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">Anything more to pay is charged to your Card on File. If the card is declined, press <b class="gd-ui">Pay and apply the change</b>.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div class="gd-t">To say no, press <b class="gd-ui">Decline this change</b>. Your booking stays as it was.</div></li></ol></div><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Tip</span><div>You have 48 hours to answer, and we send one reminder. CarmaCars signs the amendment at the moment you sign it, and the signed copy is saved under Documents. If the change costs less, the refund goes back to your card within 10 business days after the amendment is signed.</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="during-your-trip-cancel-a-booking" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Cancel a booking</h2><div class="gd-stepblock gd-stepblock--below"><div class="gd-stepcol"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">On your booking, press <b class="gd-ui">Cancel booking</b>.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Read What you get back. It shows the rule that applies and your refund.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Type the booking number to confirm (for example CC-10021), then press <b class="gd-ui">Cancel booking</b>.</div></li></ol></div><figure class="gd-fig gd-fig--desk"><div class="gd-browser"><div class="gd-bar" aria-hidden="true"><i></i><i></i><i></i><span class="gd-addr">carmacars.ca/account/bookings/CC-10003/cancel</span></div><div class="gd-imgwrap" style="aspect-ratio:1440/692"><img src="/guides/img/renter-13-cancel-desktop-d0bb2c67.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="1440" height="692"><span class="gd-pin" style="left:36.1%;top:67.2%" aria-hidden="true">2</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:95.8%;top:45.1%" aria-hidden="true">3</span></div></div></figure></div><div class="gd-tablewrap" tabindex="0" role="region" aria-label="Table"><table class="gd-table"><thead><tr><th scope="col">Standard booking: when you cancel</th><th scope="col">Refund of what you paid</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Within 24 hours of booking, and 48 hours or more before pickup</td><td>95% back</td></tr><tr><td>48 hours or more before pickup</td><td>75% back</td></tr><tr><td>24 to 48 hours before pickup</td><td>50% back</td></tr><tr><td>Less than 24 hours before pickup</td><td>No refund</td></tr></tbody></table></div><p class="gd-p">A Non-refundable booking gets no refund. The deposit is taken at pickup, so none is held when you cancel before it.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="during-your-trip-messages-tolls-and-tickets" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Messages, tolls and tickets</h2><ul class="gd-ul"><li>On a rental of 2 days or more we check in after the first day: &quot;How is the car?&quot; If anything is off, reply to the email or text, or call us.</li><li>Write to us about a booking at the bottom of its page: type in Your message and press Send.</li><li>Tolls and tickets are yours to pay, including Highway 407 ETR. If one reaches us, we pay it and charge the amount plus our fee to your Card on File, and email you a copy of the notice.</li><li>Running late? Extend in your booking, even after the return time while you still have the car, or call us at 289-312-5991. The late fee is 17.5% of the daily rate for each started hour (at least $25) after a 30 minute grace.</li><li>Before your return we remind you: the day before, about 3 hours before (with an Extend link) and at the return time. If the car is late we send a notice at 15 minutes and a final notice at 2 hours. No late notices between 10 pm and 7 am.</li><li>Already brought the car back but still getting late notices? Tap <b class="gd-ui">I&#39;ve returned the car</b> in the notice, or press it on your booking. Add photos of the car where you left it (pick several at once from your camera roll), the odometer, the fuel level and the time you returned it: all optional. The late notices stop at once while we check. When we confirm, your trip is complete. If we cannot find the car, we tell you why and the notices start again.</li><li>Something wrong with the car? While you have it, press <b class="gd-ui">Report a problem</b> on your booking: it calls roadside help, or opens a message to us.</li><li>Someone else will drive too? Press <b class="gd-ui">Add a driver</b>: write their name in the message and we add them; they sign with their own link.</li></ul></section><section class="gd-task" id="during-your-trip-return-the-car-yourself-release-28" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Return the car yourself (release 28)</h2><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">Return the car yourself</b> on your booking: photos of the car where you left it, the odometer, the fuel and the time. With all of them your trip is completed at once and any late notices stop; we may still adjust the readings after we see the car.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="during-your-trip-report-an-accident" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Report an accident</h2><p class="gd-p">While you have the car, the <b class="gd-ui">Accident card</b> on your booking has <b class="gd-ui">Report an accident</b>. Anyone hurt? Call 911 first.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Say what happened, when (empty means now) and where: type it or press <b class="gd-ui">Use my location</b>.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Add photos and videos from your camera roll: all the cars, the plates, the damage and the scene.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Add the other party&#39;s name, phone, plate and their insurer, and the police report number if there is one.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">Answer <b class="gd-ui">Is anyone hurt?</b> and <b class="gd-ui">Can the car be driven?</b>, then press <b class="gd-ui">Send the report</b>.</div></li></ol></div><p class="gd-p">Your answers stay on your phone as you type until you send them. Once sent, our team has it at once and calls you; the page shows the next steps, <b class="gd-ui">Call us</b>, and lets you add more photos or videos.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="during-your-trip-extend-at-the-same-rate-release-35" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Extend at the same rate (release 35)</h2><p class="gd-p">An extension costs the same a day as your booking, and per-trip fees such as the Protection Plan are charged for the added days at the same rate. Delivery is never charged again. The price shows before you ask.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="during-your-trip-secondary-contact-and-rideshare-documents" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Secondary contact and rideshare documents</h2><p class="gd-p">Open <b class="gd-ui">More</b> on your booking page:</p><ul class="gd-ul"><li><b class="gd-ui">Secondary contact</b>: someone we may call if we cannot reach you, for this trip or on your profile. Optional.</li><li><b class="gd-ui">Rideshare or delivery documents</b>: rideshare and delivery driving are welcome. Driving for Uber, Lyft, DoorDash, Uber Eats, Instacart or another platform? Pick the platforms and print the documents they ask for: your rental agreement, a coverage letter and a vehicle letter.</li></ul></section><section class="gd-task" id="during-your-trip-rideshare-a-second-contact-and-a-mid-trip-check-release-35" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Rideshare, a second contact and a mid-trip check (release 35)</h2><ul class="gd-ul"><li>Driving for Uber, Lyft, DoorDash, Uber Eats, Instacart or another platform is allowed: your booking page makes the documents they ask for.</li><li>Add a secondary contact we can call if we cannot reach you, on your profile or for one trip.</li><li>Halfway through a longer trip we send one short message asking how it is going. Reply with any problem and our team picks it up.</li><li>We send no automatic text at night; an answer asked for then arrives in the morning. Common questions are answered at once, and a person answers anything else.</li></ul></section><section class="gd-task" id="during-your-trip-deposit-still-owed-release-48" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Deposit still owed (release 48)</h2><p class="gd-p">If you picked up the car before the deposit hold was placed, your booking page says <b class="gd-ui">Deposit still owed</b> with the amount. It is a hold on your credit card, not a charge, released after the rental. We try your saved card each morning; if that does not work we send you a secure link by text or email. Tap it to place the hold, or call us.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="during-your-trip-notices-from-the-car-s-tracker-release-48" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Notices from the car&#39;s Tracker (release 48)</h2><p class="gd-p">Every car has a Tracker, as your rental agreement says (section 12). If it records something, we tell you at once by email, text or the app: what happened, any charge, and the clause of your agreement.</p><ul class="gd-ul"><li><b class="gd-ui">Speeding over 180, 220 or 300 km/h</b>: one speeding charge an event, at the highest limit reached ($500, $1,000 or $2,500 plus HST). It is taken from your deposit first.</li><li>A speed well over the limit, or hard braking: a friendly heads-up. No charge.</li><li><b class="gd-ui">The car outside Ontario, past its return time, or its Tracker unplugged</b>: please call us.</li><li>Leaving Canada: taking the car out of Canada always needs our written approval before you go. Ask us first.</li><li><b class="gd-ui">The car at an impound lot</b>: call us at once so we can get it released. The towing and storage costs are yours.</li></ul><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Open the notice, or your booking page.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Call us if something is wrong or you have a question. We would rather sort it out with you.</div></li></ol></div><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Note</span><div>You can turn the heads-up messages off under <b class="gd-ui">Notifications</b>. Notices about a charge are always sent.</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="during-your-trip-your-monthly-check-in-visit" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Your monthly check-in visit</h2><p class="gd-p">On a rental of about a month or longer, your trips page shows <b class="gd-ui">Next check-in visit: around</b> a date. It is a quick, free visit (about 15 minutes) so we can keep the car in top shape and catch maintenance early. Nothing to pay, and it is a suggestion, not a requirement. A few days before, we send you a reminder: press <b class="gd-ui">Pick a time</b> and choose a time at our office, or <b class="gd-ui">By request</b> with when and where suits you. You can change the time or take it back.</p></section>');
select app.guide_release_section('admin', 'maintenance-and-service', 'chapter', 'usage-and-paid-usage', 'Every real car has its service items: oil, tire rotation, brakes, tires, the seasonal swap, the safety inspection, the registration, battery, wipers, filters, alignment, fluids and the annual inspection. Record a service once and the bill is made and the timers reset by themselves.

## The fleet overview

Open **Cars** > **Maintenance**.

1. Every real car (sample cars are left out), most urgent first: overdue, then due soon, then cars with no record yet, then all OK.
2. Each car shows what is due next, its odometer, its km a day, the tires on it and the date of its last service.
3. Use Show, Service item, Sort and the search (car, plate or owner) to narrow the list, then press Apply.
4. Press **Record a service** on a car to record it without leaving the list.

| Status | Means |
| --- | --- |
| Overdue | Past its km or its date (whichever came first), or expired |
| Due soon | Within 1,000 km or 14 days of it (each item may have its own; inspections and registration: 30 days) |
| Unknown | No record yet: record the last time it was done |
| OK | Done, and not due soon |

## Record a service in one step

From the overview, the car''s **Maintenance** tab, or a To do line.

1. Tick what was done. The items due are ticked already.
2. Check the date and the odometer (filled with the current reading). Type the shop, the cost before HST and the HST (worked out at 13%, change it to match the receipt).
3. Who pays: the owner (deducted on the owner''s next statement, owner agreement 11.1; the default for an owner''s car), CarmaCars (a company expense; the default for a company car), a claim (a repair cost on the claim), the renter (a charge at cost on the rental), or no charge.
4. Leave **The bill is in: bill it now** ticked to make the bill now, or untick it and press **Bill now** on the record when the bill comes in. Add the receipt.
5. Press **Record the service**. Each item done is OK again, with its next date and km.

- An inspection or the registration: type the new expiry date, or leave it empty for 12 months from the service.
- Tires: type the tread depth measured, or tick New tires put on (the old set is retired as replaced).
- Seasonal swap: choose the set that went on and where the removed set is stored.
- An expense entered under Money, Expenses with a car and a service category (Car service: oil change, brakes, and so on) records the service too. Voiding either voids the other.
- **Void** on a record sets the timers back. A company expense is voided and an open owner cost is waived; a cost already on a statement or a claim stays, and the void is refused with what to do.

## Tires and the seasonal swap

On the car''s **Maintenance** tab, under Tires.

1. **Add a tire set**: kind (summer, all-season, winter or all-weather), size, brand, tread depth, made (DOT) and bought dates, where it is stored, and whether it is on the car.
2. **Put on the car** swaps sets and keeps the swap in the history.
3. Tires are due soon at 4 mm of tread or 5.5 years old, overdue at 3 mm or 6 years.
4. The swap follows Ontario: winter tires on by December 1 (reminder from November 1), off after April 1 (reminder from April 1, overdue after May 1). All-weather tires need no swap.

> Tip: The Winter tires add-on is offered only on cars with a winter set (on the car or stored), or with no tire record yet. A car on winter tires says so on the add-on.

## The odometer

- The current odometer is the highest reading from handover and return reports, field staff moves, the rental''s odometer out and in, listing photos, the car record, services and readings added by hand.
- Km a day comes from the readings of the last 90 days (else the rentals, else 60 km a day). It gives the date a km interval will be reached.
- **Add a reading** on the car; a reading lower than the last one needs the tick. An Admin can void a wrong reading.

## Intervals, reminders and blocks

Open **Settings** > **Maintenance**.

- Each item''s default interval: **Change**. Whichever of km and months comes first is due; 0 or empty means not by that measure.
- **Add an interval** for a class or one car. A car''s own comes first, then its class''s, then the default. On the car''s tab, **Set an interval for this car** does the same.
- Which expense categories are a service, and the items each records.
- Reminders: one Fleet task per car with what is due, To do lines (cars due, services to bill, cars with no record yet) and one line in the morning digest. No other email.
- Handover is refused while a recorded safety inspection or registration has expired. Block new bookings when overdue is off for every item until you turn it on.

Cars that were in the fleet before maintenance came in start as unknown, with one task each to record the last service. Enter what you know once.
', 'Maintenance and service', 'The fleet overview, recording a service and its bill, tires and swaps, the odometer, intervals, reminders and blocks.',
